{"baseRefName":"fix/chain-w1-v2-proof-ci-20261106","body":"## Problem\n\nThe frozen W1 recursive proof profile did not have a reproducible mapping from its concrete encodings, programs, transcript and saved v2 fixture to the premises of the CDHZ QROM reduction. A general theorem or stored digest width is insufficient to qualify this implementation.\n\n## Change\n\nThis continuation of #745 records the fixed BabyBear/extension and FRI profile, reconstructs the 27-program control tree and parameter digest, parses the saved receipt's complete seal geometry, and evaluates explicitly hypothetical CDHZ 6.10 / 8.3 component expressions with exact arithmetic. The new CI checks both the exact head and prospective merge and requires every fixed named negative control to complete.\n\nThe report preserves 15 open obligations. Authorization, proof soundness and quantum work / chain weight remain independent conclusions. All production, consensus, full-proof, quantum-work and post-quantum qualifications remain false; project quantum security bits remain null.\n\n## Exact initial source\n\n- Commit: `7150d96a2112875b4afcf3023361a5cef4a0e4b1`\n- Tree: `c8acae01f6fed538fabd918b6d7b63da348538df`\n- Base: `cb114b13bf848a77634e40a08b31b30c7c758e7b`\n- Report: [W1 QROM implementation map](https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/blob/7150d96a2112875b4afcf3023361a5cef4a0e4b1/docs/security/W1_QROM_IMPLEMENTATION_MAP_20261107.md)\n\n## Validation and limitations\n\n356 Python controls passed on the exact local committed source; Rust formatting, repository/Markdown checks, bundle verification and isolated patch tree reproduction passed. Previous offline Cargo graph, native tests and strict Clippy were blocked by missing dependencies. Complete tracked-byte source verification was blocked by unavailable inherited archive fragments; this is retained as a failure, not counted as passed.\n\nThe authenticated Hepta desktop Git channel pushed this exact commit with the repository's pre-push hook enabled and verified the remote SHA. Hosted results will be assessed independently; existing results on #745 are not attributed to this new head.\n\nThis is a draft research and evidence PR. It does not activate proof-based admission or qualify complete post-quantum PoN.","headRefName":"fix/chain-w1-qrom-implementation-map-20261107","headRefOid":"1a14f7d4826363daefac9ec10131c66d7e70ece7","isDraft":true,"number":778,"title":"W1: map frozen recursive proof profile to QROM obligations","url":"https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/pull/778"}
